<Base title="About — Isaiah Gilliland" current="About">
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow reveal r1">About</p>
      <h1 class="reveal r2">Isaiah Gilliland</h1>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="content">
    <div class="wrap about-grid">
      <figure class="about-photo reveal r2" style="margin:0">
        <img src="/assets/about/isaiah.jpg" alt="Isaiah Gilliland" />
        <figcaption>Raleigh, North Carolina</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <div class="about-prose reveal r3">
        <p class="first">I'm a technical artist and a self-taught programmer. I've been writing code for over twenty-five years, which is a long time to still get this excited about a good shader. Most of what I care about in the work comes down to one thing: keeping it simple and getting to the core of an idea.</p>
        <p>I was born in Salinas, California, one of seven children raised by a single mother &mdash; a Christian minister. We moved to Texas when I was young, to a house in the middle of a field with a creek running along one side. I didn't end up on the path that upbringing pointed me toward: I dropped out of college and went a pretty different direction. Nobody in my family did anything like this, so most of what I know I figured out on my own &mdash; usually the hard way.</p>
        <p>I got started in web development, taking contracts right out of high school. That led to a contract with Omni-Arts in Australia building a game for Intel's AppUp platform, where I wrote the Axis HTML5 engine from scratch. I had no business taking that on, and did it anyway. I've been building things ever since &mdash; games, tools, shaders, and art. I'm not sure I know how to stop.</p>
        <p>The idea underneath it all has stayed the same: find the essence of something and strip it back until only what matters is left. In code that means simplicity and elegance; in art, focusing on the subject; in a game, building around one clear idea. It's close to the Japanese notion of <em>shibumi</em> &mdash; a quiet, understated kind of beauty. Mostly, though, I just like making things, and I try not to take myself too seriously while I do it.</p>
        <p class="pf-elsewhere about-elsewhere">
          <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/isaiah-gilliland-31a79b225/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LinkedIn <span class="ext" aria-hidden="true">&#8599;</span></a>
          <span class="sep" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span>
          <a href="https://docs.google.com/document/d/12hqL5ctVS3Mkf-quU-6EgZLvYw_N6ZyQ1dfbwmF4Te8/export?format=pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Resume <span class="ext" aria-hidden="true">&#8599;</span></a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
